# Spec 07 Phase A — userKnowledge schema adoption (PERIPHERY)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before edits)
# A1 GIVEN an assessment save, WHEN userKnowledge/{uid} is read back, THEN every
#    stored answer is nested at entries.<key> with value, source:"assessment",
#    and updatedAt, and the write uses merge semantics.
# A2 GIVEN any Settings move-detail edit (date/current/new address), WHEN its
#    userKnowledge mirror completes, THEN only the edited entry is merged with
#    source:"settings" and unrelated assessment entries remain present.
# A3 GIVEN an in-app assessment-key update, WHEN its best-effort mirror runs,
#    THEN it uses the entries schema with source:"assessment".
# A4 GIVEN a test-bot entries-shaped document, WHEN contextBuilder flattens it,
#    THEN the harness returns non-empty mapped values from those entries.
# A5 GIVEN the complete Phase A diff, WHEN a fresh-context validator receives
#    this contract, the spec, diff, and build/harness evidence, THEN A1-A4 each
#    receive an evidence-backed PASS or FAIL; the writer does not self-grade.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretation)
# - The spec says four write sites: AssessmentDataManager + three Settings sites.
#   Current code instead has one AssessmentDataManager writer, one shared Settings
#   date writer, two identity-only Settings address edits, and one in-app writer.
#   Migrate every actual writer and add schema mirrors for the three Settings move
#   details (date/current/new address), preserving identity as the canonical store.
#
